WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:16.389
Unit thirty-two: Work and Meaning. In this unit, you will discuss motivation, purpose and attitudes to work.

4
00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:18.396
vocation.

5
00:00:19.096 --> 00:00:23.383
vocation means a type of work you feel especially suited to.

6
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.007
Teaching is her true vocation.

7
00:00:26.707 --> 00:00:29.592
Your turn. Say: vocation.

8
00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:33.270
vocation.

9
00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:35.029
calling.

10
00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:39.493
calling means a strong feeling that you should do a particular job.

11
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:42.060
For many nurses, caring is a calling.

12
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.493
Your turn. Say: calling.

13
00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:48.928
calling.

14
00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.672
intrinsic motivation.

15
00:00:52.372 --> 00:00:58.807
intrinsic motivation means doing something because you enjoy it or find it meaningful.

16
00:00:59.107 --> 00:01:02.105
Intrinsic motivation lasts longer than bonuses.

17
00:01:02.805 --> 00:01:06.177
Your turn. Say: intrinsic motivation.

18
00:01:08.877 --> 00:01:10.424
intrinsic motivation.

19
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.894
extrinsic reward.

20
00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:17.439
extrinsic reward means an outside reward such as money or praise.

21
00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.459
Extrinsic rewards can reduce creativity.

22
00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:24.670
Your turn. Say: extrinsic reward.

23
00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.882
extrinsic reward.

24
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:31.128
job crafting.

25
00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:35.581
job crafting means reshaping your job to make it more meaningful.

26
00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:39.506
Through job crafting, she added mentoring to her role.

27
00:01:40.206 --> 00:01:43.357
Your turn. Say: job crafting.

28
00:01:46.057 --> 00:01:47.314
job crafting.

29
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:49.631
meaningful work.

30
00:01:50.331 --> 00:01:54.293
meaningful work means work that feels important and worthwhile.

31
00:01:54.593 --> 00:01:58.078
Young people increasingly seek meaningful work.

32
00:01:58.778 --> 00:02:02.290
Your turn. Say: meaningful work.

33
00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.699
meaningful work.

34
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:08.766
quiet quitting.

35
00:02:09.466 --> 00:02:13.009
quiet quitting means doing only the minimum required at work.

36
00:02:13.309 --> 00:02:16.249
Quiet quitting became a trend after the pandemic.

37
00:02:16.949 --> 00:02:20.112
Your turn. Say: quiet quitting.

38
00:02:22.812 --> 00:02:23.883
quiet quitting.

39
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:26.047
workaholism.

40
00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:30.825
workaholism means an unhealthy need to work all the time.

41
00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:34.216
Workaholism can damage health and relationships.

42
00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:38.102
Your turn. Say: workaholism.

43
00:02:40.802 --> 00:02:41.919
workaholism.

44
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.102
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:45.402 --> 00:02:49.201
Ms. Sarah, do you see teaching as a job or a vocation?

46
00:02:50.517 --> 00:02:54.922
A vocation, definitely. Do you think you'll find yours in engineering?

47
00:02:56.217 --> 00:03:00.509
I hope so. My father didn't. He worked only for the salary.

48
00:03:01.817 --> 00:03:06.942
Many do. Extrinsic rewards matter, but rarely satisfy on their own.

49
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.494
What about quiet quitting? Some friends say they do it.

50
00:03:12.783 --> 00:03:17.769
Understandable, if their work feels meaningless. Job crafting might help.

51
00:03:19.083 --> 00:03:21.570
And workaholism is the opposite extreme.

52
00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:27.373
Exactly. Neither is healthy. Meaningful work with balance is.

53
00:03:28.683 --> 00:03:33.214
Grammar focus: Ellipsis and substitution (extended).

54
00:03:33.514 --> 00:03:36.814
Ellipsis and substitution avoid repetition.

55
00:03:37.114 --> 00:03:40.442
I hope so. My father didn't. Many do.

56
00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:43.740
They make spoken English sound natural and fluent.

57
00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:49.801
Ellipsis is natural in speech and makes conversations sound fluent rather than repetitive.

58
00:03:50.817 --> 00:03:53.469
Now read and listen. Why Do We Work?.

59
00:03:53.769 --> 00:03:57.615
For most of history, people worked simply to survive.

60
00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:04.364
Today, many also expect their work to provide purpose and identity.

61
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:11.609
Psychologists distinguish intrinsic motivation from extrinsic rewards such as salary and status.

62
00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:17.946
Research suggests that people who find their work meaningful are healthier and more productive.

63
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.059
However, not everyone has a calling, and many jobs are repetitive.

64
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:31.065
Job crafting allows employees to reshape tasks and relationships to increase meaning.

65
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.370
Trends such as quiet quitting suggest that many workers feel disconnected.

66
00:04:37.683 --> 00:04:43.154
Workaholism, on the other hand, shows that too much devotion can also be harmful.

67
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.242
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:04:47.542 --> 00:04:50.354
Doing only the minimum required at work is blank.

69
00:04:50.654 --> 00:04:55.515
A, job crafting. B, quiet quitting. C, workaholism.

70
00:04:59.517 --> 00:05:02.027
The answer is B: quiet quitting.

71
00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:06.311
'Will it rain tomorrow?' 'I hope blank.'

72
00:05:06.611 --> 00:05:09.777
A, not. B, no. C, isn't.

73
00:05:13.783 --> 00:05:15.713
The answer is A: not.

74
00:05:17.217 --> 00:05:20.458
I enjoy my job, and so blank my sister.

75
00:05:20.758 --> 00:05:24.006
A, is. B, does. C, has.

76
00:05:28.017 --> 00:05:30.283
The answer is B: does.

77
00:05:31.783 --> 00:05:34.514
An outside reward such as money is an blank.

78
00:05:34.814 --> 00:05:40.499
A, intrinsic motivation. B, extrinsic reward. C, vocation.

79
00:05:44.483 --> 00:05:47.586
The answer is B: extrinsic reward.

80
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:52.906
According to the text, people who find their work meaningful are blank.

81
00:05:53.206 --> 00:05:58.960
A, healthier and more productive. B, richer. C, more stressed.

82
00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:06.227
The answer is A: healthier and more productive.

83
00:06:07.717 --> 00:06:14.839
Now it's your turn. Part one: Is it more important to earn a high salary or to do meaningful work?

84
00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:26.086
Part two: Give your position, two reasons, and use ellipsis at least once.

85
00:06:32.386 --> 00:06:43.681
Meaningful work, for me. Money matters, of course, but it doesn't satisfy for long; meaning does. Will I always find it? I hope so, and if not, I'll try job crafting.

86
00:06:43.981 --> 00:06:46.085
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:53.288
Great work today! You learned eight new words and ellipsis and substitution (extended).

88
00:06:53.588 --> 00:06:57.820
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

89
00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.271
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

90
00:07:01.571 --> 00:07:04.525
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

